1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,137
This country is the first on Earth

2
00:00:02,137 --> 00:00:03,520
to see every new year.

3
00:00:03,870 --> 00:00:06,222
Kiribati is a nation in the middle

4
00:00:06,222 --> 00:00:09,127
of the Pacific Ocean, made of thirty-three

5
00:00:09,127 --> 00:00:10,441
islands and atolls.

6
00:00:10,791 --> 00:00:13,423
Its islands are spread across about three

7
00:00:13,423 --> 00:00:15,927
and a half million square kilometers of

8
00:00:15,927 --> 00:00:18,881
ocean, wider than the whole continental United

9
00:00:18,881 --> 00:00:21,193
States. But all its land together is

10
00:00:21,193 --> 00:00:23,376
smaller than New York City and its

11
00:00:23,376 --> 00:00:23,889
suburbs.

12
00:00:24,239 --> 00:00:27,139
It's also the only country that sits

13
00:00:27,139 --> 00:00:30,602
in all four hemispheres: north, south, east

14
00:00:30,602 --> 00:00:33,582
and west, because it crosses both the

15
00:00:33,582 --> 00:00:36,079
equator and the 180th meridian.

16
00:00:36,429 --> 00:00:39,077
For a long time, the International Date

17
00:00:39,077 --> 00:00:42,065
Line ran right through Kiribati. Its eastern

18
00:00:42,065 --> 00:00:44,984
and western islands were on different days.

19
00:00:45,334 --> 00:00:48,411
So in 1995, Kiribati moved its eastern

20
00:00:48,411 --> 00:00:50,839
islands to the same day as the

21
00:00:50,839 --> 00:00:53,592
rest of the country. The date line

22
00:00:53,592 --> 00:00:55,211
now bends around it.

23
00:00:55,561 --> 00:00:58,975
That put the Line Islands, including Kiritimati,

24
00:00:58,975 --> 00:01:01,961
or Christmas Island, at UTC plus fourteen,

25
00:01:01,961 --> 00:01:04,735
the earliest time zone on Earth. That's

26
00:01:04,735 --> 00:01:07,295
why they welcome the New Year first.

27
00:01:07,645 --> 00:01:10,108
And there's a serious side. Most of

28
00:01:10,108 --> 00:01:12,571
Kiribati is only a few meters above

29
00:01:12,571 --> 00:01:14,753
sea level, so rising seas are a

30
00:01:14,753 --> 00:01:16,583
real threat to its future.

31
00:01:16,933 --> 00:01:19,731
Meanwhile, the last places on Earth to

32
00:01:19,731 --> 00:01:22,454
reach the New Year are American Samoa

33
00:01:22,454 --> 00:01:26,282
and some uninhabited islands, about twenty-six hours

34
00:01:26,282 --> 00:01:27,387
after Kiribati.

35
00:01:27,737 --> 00:01:31,018
Kiritimati is one of the largest coral

36
00:01:31,018 --> 00:01:33,867
atolls on Earth by land area, and

37
00:01:33,867 --> 00:01:36,890
it was named by Captain James Cook,

38
00:01:36,890 --> 00:01:39,998
who landed there on Christmas Eve in

39
00:01:39,998 --> 00:01:40,430
1777.

40
00:01:40,780 --> 00:01:43,457
Merry Christmas from Earth Decoded! Where will

41
00:01:43,457 --> 00:01:45,378
you be when the New Year arrives?

42
00:01:45,378 --> 00:01:46,775
Tell me in the comments.

